From c85515b88779af4f439a3727a39f35d7089487b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:20:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/29] media: fimc-is2: end the format enumeration of the
 camera nodes

The VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT handlers of the fimc-is video nodes are stubs that
return 0 for every index without filling anything in.  A V4L2 client that
enumerates formats until EINVAL never gets there: FFmpeg's v4l2m2m wrapper
scans every /dev/video* node and spins on the first fimc-is one (with a
kernel warning about an unknown pixel format on each call), and so would
any program listing cameras.

The stubs now return -EINVAL, which is "no formats" for the caller.  The
vendor camera HAL cannot have relied on a successful enumeration, since a
loop over it never ended.

Signed-off-by: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
